's popular dishes the  blue crab toast we're going to make the  lemon caper ravigote it's a fancy way  for sand lemon horseradish mayonnaise  horseradish scallions mustard lemon  juice mayo and lump crab meat on toasted  brioche and then we have our avocado and  lemon  juice salt and pepper and we take that  and we just do a nice little  [Applause]  [Music]  that's our blue crabs there it is check  that out look at this  i did it all by myself  you enjoy a nice a nice evening of  dinner and then come next door into the  jazz club to listen to a set of music  the front of the house is robert's  domain the wharton grad mimics the  60-year career of his late father  benjamin bynum senior he owned the  cadillac club which later became impulse  posting the likes of aretha franklin  nina simone and fats domino when you  think about your dad's club and what it  meant  to the folks who were employed there to  the community that it served  what was it that it provided that  no place else could  the impulse was at broad germantown  which might be considered to be a  low-income area and he made a commitment  to the community to have a place that  was upscale elegant and treated people  in a manner that they  might not be treated every place so they  really felt like it was a refuge within  the community so service was  really important to your family very  much so i mean it was a safe haven kind  of for us um you know we grew up at that  time uh it's in the heart of north  philadelphia it used to be called  yorktown  it was  a challenging area but i think that  it was a place where people enjoyed  getting dressed up and going which was a  little bit unusual for those times since  1990 the brothers picked up the reigns  with six restaurants in philadelphia  including zanzibar blue open from 1990  to 2007. you opened the club when jazz  was on the decline  how much part of keeping that tradition  alive was zanzibar blue  philadelphia has a rich jazz tradition  and we felt like things have begun to  slide a little bit so we were very  committed to presenting  upscale  environment with really big names we did  blue raws we did chichoria we've done  jimmy scott we've done nancy wilson so  we were really committed to bringing  back jazz to the city of philadelphia  benjamin bynum senior also worked with  his sons at their longest running eatery  warm daddies he died at the age of 98  just last year he uh handled our door at  warren daddy's for for many many years  he only stopped  probably a year or so before he passed  away and he was very much our rock he  was very much who we relied on to bounce  ideas off and to be supportive of what  we were doing  so it was a loss but we still have his  legacy to hold on to the brothers  decided to close warm daddies during the  pandemic but continue to serve up food  and music at relish and here at south  the ultimate celebration of their  father's legacy business is good  people are coming back people are coming  back the vaccine mandate has been lifted  the mass mandate has just been lifted in  philadelphia so that's really made a big  difference to folks and people are  coming out and i think the feeling  beginning to feel a lot more comfortable  really we've been fortunate to have a  very loyal clientele that supports us at  all of our venues so  that's something that is uh  been reassuring to us  [Music]  and nothing gets those guys too excited  i mean they're very even keel it's how  they run the business and how they've  been able to run it for so long of  course i brought you some goodies here  we have everything from mac and cheese  to their cornbread the blue crab toast  that i  made myself  deviled eggs there's catfish and and uh  shrimp and seafood bouillabaisse but the  one thing they did not bring was my  absolute or sin was my absolute favorite  why what was the pineapple bread pudding  oh the best bread pudding i have ever  had i love bread pudding folks in new  orleans uh i got something to tell you  what i hate to break that news to you  was better than new orleans own what  whoa i'm not kidding you michelle  talking smack about your life i'm  talking smack about my what do we got  here is this a side car oh this yeah  styling cheers cheers folks cheers nice  to have you here jamie nice piece  michelle thank you

